  "worked_solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $2$ and $4:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14057099/assets/849f44d06de55f14811d433f9ccfdd30d47f6a1db1970cdfbfbd6f16be4959b0.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$",
